#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046669} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558708} :activity/id #uuid "690ad7aa-ab30-56bf-bea8-00d3dcd607d3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050741 :topic/id #uuid "62cde46f-1bc8-533b-b62a-02ec7aac97f3" :topic/math-academy-id 4174} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558614 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17408f30-0e49-5024-8582-e77ea33d1531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435420} {:answer/id #uuid "1aa03666-f99f-5788-82b2-6a8cfc4ed4a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435421} {:answer/id #uuid "5c870d2c-e72b-5ed4-9ac6-a6bac8e306d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435430} {:answer/id #uuid "c3244fd4-d2f9-5e9c-ab2f-2bf3f05ed94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435447} {:answer/id #uuid "dac54592-73f2-5539-95af-9b181dfbbc6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435452}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435452} :answer-field/id #uuid "96a67bd8-ef2e-5ca9-867f-c8028ad58f33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3441cc98-9576-5e74-bdad-b0f5fae54049" :question/math-academy-id "q-163607" :question/problem "A plate of mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ bounded by the lines $y=2x,$ $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis. Its mass density at any point on the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{3M}{2}x.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function. The region $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x\\}.\n$$\n\nHence, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{3M}{2}x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2x}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}x{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{4}+\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{14}{3}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{[\\frac{14}{15}{x}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{14}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{0} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7M}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3a47ba87-f12b-5d88-a549-0d6d86da790e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558626}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558626 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "901a1aa5-f9b9-54e8-b4e1-ed9066218fc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{7}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435441} {:answer/id #uuid "91a40d38-352d-5174-8eee-24d0d573f67c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435442} {:answer/id #uuid "a72adde0-d637-5df5-9d74-b56a66f4cfac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{41}{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435445} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f45d1c-6eee-552d-b559-5553e3c33b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435448} {:answer/id #uuid "d7589253-2194-5059-b7cf-fc834480c4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435451}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435442} :answer-field/id #uuid "6481d0c5-9b18-592d-a5aa-357b3fbca57b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435461}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9f4fdbea-b5e1-5c4f-b10b-d88e66b48be2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163610" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,3\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,2\\le y\\le 4\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{3}^{5}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{3}^{5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(\\frac{125}{3}-9)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{98}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{[\\frac{98}{3}y]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{49M}{6}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{49M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{49}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{3}}=\\frac{7}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5be9f89f-879b-5095-b096-6255f6ab38f0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558637}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558637 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198665 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e41b76a-dabb-5807-a6bb-5779e0a43c8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278869} {:answer/id #uuid "59d4646c-a8cc-5cc4-8c20-a790ad2f4d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279413} {:answer/id #uuid "74959f37-361c-597f-97f4-79fda9c4ad64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279642} {:answer/id #uuid "ed79e371-e80a-5031-880e-b39448d43e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280675} {:answer/id #uuid "ee046b1f-ca21-54a9-88ec-7eeb4e214626" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280677}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280675} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee676f82-5c11-53e9-9b1a-845255b4b041" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281256}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2496e287-b250-5877-a40c-af954399de62" :question/math-academy-id "q-163612" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,4\\le y\\le 6\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\frac{1}{3}(1-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}[y]_{4}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(6-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6ebe3ba1-9fbe-5010-bd90-9adc46f51310"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558683 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281677 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8c3f43-d62e-5000-aa73-65488d3b0b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278693} {:answer/id #uuid "124a91eb-fdf5-5e37-9d33-f96d11c8d50d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278758} {:answer/id #uuid "4cbbd3c2-db9a-55d6-97d8-e5b35b4b7f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279281} {:answer/id #uuid "6f8c9571-4624-5e8c-9ba9-3cb3cfed6da9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279604} {:answer/id #uuid "d0235cb5-d166-53f6-8c2a-e428ad59a7f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280423}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280423} :answer-field/id #uuid "65cfd582-049a-5c5a-85d6-152e3b8591a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c52b9e07-a1a1-59e3-9b59-f3ce7c050afb" :question/math-academy-id "q-163578" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 3=3.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}(1+9) \\\\  & =\\frac{10M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{10}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c1368fa6-248d-5ee3-a8cf-6aa3d64b5c88" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558614}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558708 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198651 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06aa15d2-30ee-5cc9-b5dd-ac324e05cd6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278654} {:answer/id #uuid "240de7aa-73fc-57f0-b478-71f4546ac6b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278914} {:answer/id #uuid "578364b4-8440-58d4-999a-e71df76621b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{16}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279394} {:answer/id #uuid "8474f088-76e4-5da5-a9e4-54e62eda057e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279781} {:answer/id #uuid "8f9f0418-d641-5bc4-9599-2fdec0a94b81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279869}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278654} :answer-field/id #uuid "2413e5c4-0b04-5b4f-a226-389f725261b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5e1eb104-83e6-5dc7-913b-3996107f92c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-163011" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{4}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(4+9-(\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(13-\\frac{5}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{34}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{17}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ed323905-6ae2-5d53-bd0a-b0c0821630d1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558683}}] :activity/title "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557864}]}
